# Not needed to build/run Direwolf inside the image; keeping them out of the
# build context is what actually matters for docker build speed (final
# image size is controlled by the multi-stage COPY list in Dockerfile,
# not by this file).
.git
.claude
referenceDir
release
benchmark
test
docs
report
fort.*

# Build artifacts. Docker's .dockerignore does NOT treat a bare "build"
# as "match at every level" the way .gitignore does, so each artifact
# path is listed explicitly. If these get COPY'd in, a from-scratch
# `make` inside the image finds a stale, wrong-arch libxcf03.a / *.mod
# already in place and skips rebuilding - cross-arch builds (e.g. armv7
# on an x86 host) then fail with "Type mismatch ... INTEGER(4) to
# INTEGER(8)" from the leftover x86 libxc .mod.
#
# NOTE: do NOT use "**/build" here - it also matches the real vendored
# source directory third_party/toml-f/src/tomlf/build/, whose removal
# breaks toml-f's cmake ("add_subdirectory given source 'build' which is
# not an existing directory"). The anchored "third_party/*/build" hits
# only the one-level cmake build dirs the vendored libs actually use.
/build
third_party/*/build
third_party/_install
third_party/OpenBLAS/*.a
**/*.mod
**/*.o
